 to $9$ modulo $13.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9]_{13} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,13)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=9+13k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={9+13k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,9-2\\cdot 13,\\,9-13,\\,9,\\,9+13,\\,9+2\\cdot 13,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-17,-4,9,22,35,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-17$ and $35$ belong to $[9]_{13},$ while $4$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412972 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412943 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412972 1069 "q-78597" 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412972 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412972 1071 "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[-7]_{11}?$\n\n- $15$\n- $-4$\n- $7$" 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412972 1072 #uuid "abd84654-ac2d-58a6-9574-529f2b4aa6f5" 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412972 1074 "The residue class $[-7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-7]_{11} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=-7+11k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={-7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,-7-2\\cdot 11,\\,-7-11,\\,-7,\\,-7+11,\\,-7+2\\cdot 11,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-29,-18,-7,4,15,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $15$ belongs to $[-7]_{11},$ while $-4$ and $7$ do not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412930 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412931 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412938 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412944 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412947 13194139534167 17592186045417 true] [17592186412973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412951 13194139534167 17592186045